  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In February 2026 testimony, Chang said federal action is needed so new large loads pay their fair share and do not shift costs to other customers. In July 2026, she said a pressing mandate is to set clear rules enabling interconnection of new large loads while protecting existing customers from reliability risks and unwarranted cost shifts, and noted that large computational loads have major grid reliability implications. She also said integrating and serving large loads creates challenges and exacerbates existing grid problems but presents an opportunity to modernize the aging system to improve reliability and efficiency.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
